        "text_J8c8tJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>A Simple Fix for a Common Cat Problem</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "text_Urc8Hy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>If you’ve spent any time with cats, you already know their obsession with small, enclosed spaces. Boxes, paper bags, laundry baskets—you name it, they’ll jump in. Over my ten years of working with cats and helping pet parents choose enrichment products, I’ve learned that this isn’t just quirky behavior—it’s instinct. Cats seek out safe spaces to hide, rest, and stalk imaginary prey.</p><p>That’s where a cat pop up tent or a cat tube comes in. These portable, collapsible hideouts combine the safety of a retreat with the fun of a play tunnel. Whether you’re looking to give your cat a private nap spot, an indoor playground, or a way to travel with comfort, pop up tents and tubes are an affordable, space-saving solution.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
