    "rich_text_7GJRRB": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_Q6cWLY": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Indoor Uses: Play, Privacy, and Peace</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_faMV36": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A cat pop up tent or tube is more than just an accessory—it can transform your cat’s daily routine indoors.</p><ul><li><strong>Private nap spot:</strong> Place it in a quiet corner with a blanket, and it becomes your cat’s personal bedroom.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Interactive play zone:</strong> Add dangling toys or sprinkle a little catnip inside. Tubes, in particular, become highways for zoomies.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Household harmony:</strong> If you have multiple pets, providing each cat their own tent or tube can reduce conflicts by giving everyone their own “territory.”<br/><br/></li></ul><p>I’ve fostered cats who never felt safe enough to sleep in the open. As soon as I introduced a pop up tent, they finally rested without stress. It’s a simple fix for anxious cats.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_Q6cWLY",
        "text_faMV36"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich-text.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "color_scheme": "",
        "full_width": true,
        "padding_top": 40,
        "padding_bottom": 52
      }
    },
    "rich_text_8atpqp": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_7jTBtL": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Outdoor and Travel Benefits</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_cE7LyU": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>While tents are more common outdoors, cat tubes can also work in safe, supervised environments.</p><ul><li><strong>Balcony use:</strong> Place a tube on your balcony so your cat can lounge and watch the world.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Travel companion:</strong> Because they fold flat, tubes are perfect for hotel stays, road trips, or visits to relatives. Your cat gets a familiar hideout in an unfamiliar space.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Supervised outdoor fun:</strong> Some models include stakes or reinforced bottoms, letting you use them briefly in the yard.<br/><br/></li></ul><p>Important note: These are not predator-proof. Never leave your cat unattended outdoors, even in a sturdy tent or tube.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_7jTBtL",
        "text_cE7LyU"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich-text.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "color_scheme": "",
        "full_width": true,
