    "rich_text_6r4c3W": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_NaVtVa": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Training Your Cat to Love Their New Tent or Tube</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_6w7drF": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Some cats take to a tube instantly. Others need encouragement. Here’s my tried-and-true process:</p><ol><li><strong>Introduce indoors:</strong> Set it up in a familiar room. Don’t force your cat inside—let curiosity do the work.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Use positive reinforcement:</strong> Toss treats or toys inside, or rub a little catnip on the interior.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Play interactively:</strong> Drag a wand toy through the tunnel to trigger chasing behavior.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Keep sessions short at first:</strong> Build up your cat’s confidence gradually.<br/><br/></li></ol><p>With this approach, I’ve never had a cat ignore a pop up tent for more than a few days.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_NaVtVa",
        "text_6w7drF"
      ],
