    "rich_text_wVWxnC": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_xVMrXT": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>FAQs </strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_G6zn6q": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>1. Is a cat pop up tent or tube safe for kittens?<br/></strong> Yes! Tubes and tents are great for kittens—they encourage play and provide safe hiding spots. Just supervise to make sure small kittens don’t get tangled in hanging toys.</p><p><strong>2. Can I use a cat tube outdoors?<br/></strong> You can, but only under supervision. They’re not predator-proof. For outdoor use, set it up in a shaded, enclosed area and always keep an eye on your cat.</p><p><strong>3. How do I clean a cat tube?<br/></strong> Most tubes can be vacuumed for fur and spot-cleaned with mild soap and water. Some models come with removable mats or washable bases for easier care.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
